The Fichajes table in the admin panel had no filtering, sorting, or export capabilities. This adds a full interactive layer on top of the existing Firestore real-time listener without touching any other section.

## HTML
- Filter bar injected inside `.tcard` above the table: free-text search (nombre/email/dpto), tipo select, department select (auto-populated), date-range inputs, clear button, CSV download button

## CSS
- `.fichajes-filters` flex bar with consistent `--bg`/`--border`/`--accent` variables
- `th.sortable` + `.sort-asc`/`.sort-desc` for ▲/▼ visual feedback
- `.col-check` / `input[type="checkbox"]` with `accent-color: var(--accent)`

## JavaScript refactor
`loadFichajes()` now only stores the snapshot and delegates rendering:

```js
fichajesUnsub = db.collection('fichajes')
  .orderBy('timestamp', 'desc').limit(300)
  .onSnapshot(snap => {
    fichajesData = snap.docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, data: d.data() }));
    renderFichajes();
  });
```

Key additions:
- **`applyFilters(items)`** — single shared filter predicate used by both `renderFichajes()` and `descargarCSV()`
- **`fmtJornada(f)`** — shared formatting helper
- **`renderFichajes()`** — filters → sorts by `sortCol`/`sortDir` → rebuilds `<tbody>` with per-row checkboxes + select-all + sort-header click listeners
- **`descargarCSV()`** — exports checked rows, falling back to all filtered rows; UTF-8 BOM CSV named `fichajes_YYYY-MM-DD.csv`
- All filter inputs call `renderFichajes()` on `input`/`change`

