Pasting a wallet address with leading/trailing whitespace (common from clipboard) stored the raw value in the DB. On the next login without whitespace, the lookup missed the existing user and created a fresh account — losing all fighters and progress, making the game appear broken.

## Changes

- **`connect.tsx`**: Trim the address before calling `connect()` and writing to `localStorage`, so the normalized value is used consistently from the start.
- **`auth.ts`**: Trim the wallet address server-side after parsing and reject empty-after-trim values with an explicit `400`, providing defense-in-depth independent of the client.

```ts
// Before
if (!address.trim()) return;
localStorage.setItem("walletAddress", address);      // stores raw (possibly padded) value
connect({ data: { walletAddress: address } });        // sends raw value to DB

// After
const trimmedAddress = address.trim();
if (!trimmedAddress) return;
localStorage.setItem("walletAddress", trimmedAddress);
connect({ data: { walletAddress: trimmedAddress } }); // consistent, normalized value
```

